NAVIGATION (the unit is (unrouted)):
The web `TriggerConfigurator` is a CONTROLLED COMPONENT the automation builder renders inside its
step card — NOT a standalone route. So this unit does NOT take a top-level `AppRoute`. Instead it
ships a typed `NavigationDestination` seam — `TriggerConfiguratorLink` +
`View.triggerConfiguratorDestination()` + `TriggerConfiguratorRouteRegistration.make(...)` — that
any `NavigationStack` (a future builder route / macOS detail column) adopts to deep-link the
full-screen configurator. No edits to the P4 shell (AppShell/AppRoute/TeslaSyncApp) were made —
correct for an unrouted unit and consistent with the predecessor-bypass rule (covenant #7).

PREDECESSOR REUSE (no predecessor bypass — covenant #7; DRY):
A sibling component-parity surface already ships the same web source's editing logic at
`apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/TriggerConfigurator.*` (parity unit feature-views/0086). It is
PURE, view-free, public logic in the SAME module: `AutomationTrigger`(+`.createDefault` ==
web `createDefaultTrigger`), `TriggerKind`, `SignalTrigger`/`SignalValue`, `CronExpression`
(buildCronExpr/parseCronExpr), `TriggerAdapter` (handleDayToggle/signalValueFromInput/displayValue),
the option catalogs (Vehicle/Geofence/SignalOperator/Signal/Timezone/Weekday/TriggerType + boolFieldKeys),
the `Geofence` wire model, the `GeofenceSource`/`InMemoryGeofenceSource`/`GeofenceInput`/`GeofenceResolved`/
`GeofenceProjection` query seam, and the `@Observable TriggerConfiguratorModel` (all web-faithful edit
methods + the useGeofences binding). This PAGE REUSES that logic (no redefinition → zero symbol
collisions, DRY) and adds only the page-level surface: a page state holder
(`TriggerConfiguratorPageModel`) that layers trigger-KIND switching (the web parent's TRIGGER_TYPES +
createDefaultTrigger), page chrome (TSGlassPanel + nav), and NEW per-kind editor views.
WHY NEW VIEWS (not the sibling's): the sibling resolves its 21 strings from a per-surface
`TCStrings`/"TriggerConfigurator" .strings table; this PAGE's contract requires every visible literal
to resolve from the master `Localizable.xcstrings` catalog (ADR-014). So the page's editor views
render via `TrigCfgStrings.text(key, fallback)` = `NSLocalizedString(key, tableName: nil, …)` (the
default `Localizable` table) and all keys are added to `Localizable.xcstrings`. The sibling's view
files are NOT touched.

